---
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
import { urls } from "../lib/urls";
---
<MarketingLayout
  title="What Is a Kitchen Display System (KDS)?"
  description="A kitchen display system replaces printed kitchen tickets with a live digital queue. Here's how a KDS works and how it connects to POS and order status displays."
  path="/what-is-a-kitchen-display-system"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / What Is a Kitchen Display System?</p>
      <h1>What is a kitchen display system?</h1>
      <p>
        A kitchen display system (KDS) replaces printed order tickets with a live digital queue on a kitchen
        screen. When an order is placed — at the counter, through QR ordering, or takeaway — it appears on the
        relevant kitchen screen immediately, with status updates (new, preparing, ready) that flow back to the
        front of house.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--cream">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Why it matters</h2>
      <p>
        Paper tickets can be lost, miscommunicated, or hard to prioritize during a rush. A KDS gives kitchen staff
        a single live view of everything in progress, and gives front-of-house staff visibility into how far along
        an order is — feeding directly into tools like an <a href="/features/order-status-display">order status
        display</a> for customers.
      </p>
      <h2>See it on Vyfoo</h2>
      <p>Read the full <a href="/features/kitchen-display-system">Kitchen Display System</a> product page for capabilities.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--ink">
    <div class="container cta-split">
      <div><h2>See a kitchen display in action</h2></div>
      <a class="btn btn--on-ink btn--lg" href={urls.bookDemo}>Book Enterprise Demo</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
